# CLAUDE.md — {project_name}

This file mirrors `AGENTS.md` for Claude Code. OpenCode reads `AGENTS.md`
directly; Claude Code reads this file. Both share the same
`.callmem/memory.db` and callmem MCP server. Where this file and the global
`~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md` conflict, this file wins.

See `AGENTS.md` for the full coding norms, git discipline, code style, error
handling, testing, SQL, and sensitive-data rules. The callmem memory workflow
and startup briefing instructions are also documented there.

In short:
- Read `AGENTS.md` first — it is the source of truth.
- Both you (Claude Code) and OpenCode sessions write to the same memory DB.
- Run `callmem briefing` at the start of every session.
- Call `mem_session_start` to register the session.
- Cite memory entity IDs (e.g. `#F5AVDQ25`) when they inform your work.
